iption: >\n      Compute 4 detection signals on all contaminated + clean models from exp-001:\n      (a) embedding-based semantic retrieval (FAISS + sentence-transformers),\n      (b) Min-K%++ membership inference,\n      (c) ConStat performance gap (original vs paraphrased items),\n      (d) Self-Critique entropy collapse.\n      Output: per-model-item exposure scores for each signal.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 20\n    deps: [exp-001]\n\n  - id: exp-003\n    name: rrf_aggregation_ablation\n    claim: [2]\n    description: >\n      RRF fusion of 4 signals into composite per-item exposure score.\n      Ablations: (a) RRF vs equal-weight rank averaging, (b) single-signal only\n      (×4), (c) calibration-based weighted RRF variant, (d) false positive\n      injection robustness check (inject FP at rates matching Duan et al. 2024).\n      Also test degraded 2-signal mode (ConStat + Self-Critique) for closed-weight.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: [exp-002]\n\n  - id: exp-004\n    name: simulation_identifiability_sweep\n    claim: [1, 3]\n    description: >\n      Systematic synthetic-data sweep (NEW, not MVP — MVP only covered 4-5 conditions):\n      exposure signal AUC (0.55, 0.60, 0.65, 0.70, 0.80, 0.90) ×\n      model count (20, 50, 100, 200) ×\n      prior strength (N(0,0.5), N(0,1), N(0,2)) ×\n      exposure type (binary, continuous).\n      144 conditions, 10 seeds each. Reports: θ-γ recovery RMSE, posterior\n      correlation, coverage (50%/80%/95%), prior sensitivity. Establishes\n      minimum AUC threshold; if 95% CI width > 15pp at AUC=0.65, label as\n      \"cannot distinguish no contamination from moderate contamination.\"\n      N_items=300 fixed (per MVP finding).\n      Subsumes exp-010 (prior sensitivity) and exp-011 (few-examinee regime)\n      — prior × N_models dimensions already in sweep grid. Growing Pains\n      pre-estimation sub-experiment: at N_models=20/50, compare flat prior\n      vs informative prior from pre-estimated item parameters.\n      Also includes Fisher Information matrix analysis: derive approximate\n      analytical relationship between signal AUC, N_models, and γ\n      recoverability. Distinguish structural identifiability (parameters\n      uniquely determined) from practical identifiability (estimation\n      quality sufficient for decisions). Provides theoretical grounding\n      for the empirical AUC ≥ 0.70 threshold.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: []\n    note: CPU only. MVP (mvp_sim_4pl_gamma) was preliminary; this is the full sweep.\n\n  - id: exp-005\n    name: noise_propagation_analysis\n    claim: [3]\n    description: >\n      Two parts:\n      (A) Measurement error model (PRIMARY): extend Stan model to treat exposure\n      as noisy observation: exposure_ij ~ N(τ_ij, σ_e²), where τ is latent true\n      contamination. σ_e estimated from exp-001 ground truth FP/FN rates.\n      This propagates Stage 1 uncertainty into posteriors automatically.\n      Compare coverage (50%/80%/95%) vs point-estimate exposure baseline.\n      (B) Post-hoc noise injection: inject Gaussian noise at 1×/1.5×/2× matched\n      levels, re-fit standard model, measure CI widening for γ and θ.\n      Both parts inform whether measurement error model closes the coverage gap.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [exp-002, exp-004]\n    note: CPU only\n\n  - id: exp-006\n    name: irt_calibration_and_baselines\n    claim: [1, 3]\n    description: >\n      Fit 4PL+γ IRT (Stan NUTS) on controlled models from exp-001/003.\n      TWO model variants: (a) global γ (single γ across all benchmarks),\n      (b) per-benchmark γ_k (separate γ per benchmark). Report both.\n      Per-benchmark γ_k addresses Dream reviewer concern about benchmark-\n      heterogeneous contamination effects (3× range in inflation).\n      IRT fitted per-benchmark (not jointly) to reduce local independence\n      violation scope. Posterior predictive checks on item-level residual\n      correlations to assess local independence empirically.\n      Compute calibrated scores via exposure=0 counterfactual with CIs.\n      Compare against 7 baselines:\n      (0) Raw — no adjustment (anchor),\n      (1) remove-and-rescore (drop flagged items),\n      (2) single-signal 2PL+γ (best signal only, simpler IRT),\n      (3) vanilla 4PL without γ (standard IRT, no contamination modeling),\n      (4) linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI (simplest post-hoc),\n      (5) Emperor's mitigation: rephrasing + option shuffling,\n      (6) DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025) — the only existing method\n          producing adjusted accuracy; must include or reviewers will reject.\n      Evaluate all 5 metrics: MAE, coverage (50%/80%/95%), sharpness,\n      Kendall τ, dose-response monotonicity.\n      Report mean ± std across 3 seeds (matched to exp-001 seeds).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n    deps: [exp-003]\n    benchmarks: [MMLU, GSM8K, ARC-Challenge, HumanEval]\n    seeds: 3\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # P1: Important — run if time/GPU permit\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - id: exp-007\n    name: scale_bridging_7b\n    claim: [1]\n    description: >\n      Qwen2.5-7B controlled SFT injection at 5 dosage levels.\n      Validates calibration accuracy scales to larger models.\n      Requires multi-GPU node (7B LoRA SFT ~4-8h per run on 1×H100).\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 30\n    deps: [exp-001]\n\n  - id: exp-008\n    name: signal_survival_analysis\n    claim: [2]\n    description: >\n      Systematic evaluation of detection signal reliability across training regimes.\n      Signal × regime AUC heatmap: 4 signals × {base, SFT-clean, SFT-contaminated,\n      RL-post-trained}. Confirms Self-Critique compensates where Min-K%++/ConStat\n      degrade post-RL (per fragility paper arXiv 2510.02386).\n      ELEVATED to Core Contribution 2 per Dream review (all 3 tiers identified\n      this as the most genuinely novel finding).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n    deps: [exp-002]\n\n  - id: exp-014\n    name: multi_family_validation\n    claim: [1]\n    description: >\n      Controlled SFT injection on at least one non-Qwen model family\n      (Llama-3.2-1B or Pythia-1.4B) at 3 dosage levels (0%, 25%, 100%).\n      Validates that identifiability boundaries and calibration accuracy\n      generalize beyond Qwen2.5. Addresses Dream reviewer concern about\n      single model family limiting generalizability (flagged [M][W]).\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n    deps: [exp-001]\n\n  - id: exp-009\n    name: rl_observational_case_study\n    claim: [2, 3]\n    description: >\n      Apply Self-Critique + available signals to existing RL-trained models:\n      Qwen2.5-Instruct (0.5B/1.5B/3B/7B), DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B/7B.\n      Fit IRT with appropriately wider CIs. Expected regret quantification:\n      compare uncalibrated vs calibrated vs remove-rescore for top-5 model\n      selection. Framed as observational — directional external validity,\n      not full quantitative validation. Near-zero γ check on known-clean\n      benchmark (specificity test).\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n    deps: [exp-006, exp-008]\n\n  # exp-010 (prior_sensitivity) and exp-011 (few_examinee_regime) merged into exp-004.\n  # Prior × N_models dimensions already covered in the sweep grid.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # P2: Bonus — adds breadth if resources allow\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - id: exp-012\n    name: observational_72b\n    claim: [1]\n    description: >\n      Qwen2.5-72B observational analysis (inference only, no SFT).\n      Extends ecological validity to frontier model scale.\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n    deps: [exp-006]\n\n  - id: exp-013\n    name: closed_weight_2signal_mode\n    claim: [2]\n    description: >\n      Degraded 2-signal mode (ConStat + Self-Critique, no logits/embeddings)\n      for closed-weight models. Ablation quantifying 2-signal vs 4-signal\n      calibration accuracy gap.\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n    deps: [exp-003]\n\n# ============================================================\n# GPU Budget Summary\n# ============================================================\ngpu_budget:\n  P0_hours: 90\n  P1_hours: 60\n  P2_hours: 20\n  buffer_hours: 30\n  total_hours: 200\n  note: >\n    CPU-only experiments (exp-004, exp-005, exp-011) excluded.\n    Buffer covers reruns, debugging, multi-seed overhead, and unexpected issues.\n    Requires 2-4× H100/A100-80G for parallel SFT runs.\n    EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25 sprint (12 days from May 13):\n    - With 4× H100: P0 in ~4 days, P1 in ~3 days, total ~8 days (fits deadline)\n    - With 2× H100: P0 in ~7 days, P1 in ~4 days, tight but feasible if parallelized\n    - Day-8 contingency: reduce benchmarks to MMLU + GSM8K if behind schedule\n\n# Multi-seed protocol:\n# - exp-001, exp-006: 3 seeds, report mean ± std for key metrics\n# - exp-004, exp-005, exp-011: 10 seeds (simulation, CPU)\n# - exp-007, exp-008, exp-009: 1 seed (resource-constrained, note as limitation if needed)\n","numLines":245,"startLine":1,"totalLines":245}}}
